WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:06.190
Have you ever been out late at night, and
had the irrational feeling something… was

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.190
out there?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:13.429
After all, who knows what lurks in the darkness
beyond our senses…These dudes.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:14.830
These dudes are out there lurking.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.290
But, okay, what are these things supposed
to be?

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.409
What ‘evidence’ for their existence is
allegedly out there?

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:25.179
And if one fell over — could it get back
up?

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:30.650
All these vital questions and more shall be
answered, in this entry into the Archive.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.220
Our story begins in 2007, when an unknown
individual living in Fresno, California checked

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.059
their backyard security camera and allegedly,
discovered… this.

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:44.539
What looks like a pair of pants, just going
for a stroll.

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:49.230
This blurry video was the internet’s first
glance at the unusual and frankly hilarious

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.120
cryptid now known as the Fresno Nightcrawler.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.539
For those of you who don’t know, the term
cryptid refers to any organism whose existence

00:00:57.539 --> 00:00:59.739
hasn’t been proven by science.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:04.180
As you can imagine, the sheer strangeness
of these supposed cryptids compared to the

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:09.180
more familiar ones, like, say the loch ness
monster, has captured the imagination of many

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.030
individuals on the internet — and might
I just say, that I completely understand.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.229
Allegedly, Nightcrawlers stand at around three
feet tall, with a white body and disproportionately

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:20.520
long legs.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.290
Most portrayals of the creature created in
reaction to the footage portray the being

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:28.860
with two black eyes, which can’t be discerned
in the original video due to poor quality.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.890
But this blurry movie isn’t the only evidence
of the supposed organism.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:36.000
We also have… this other blurry video!

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.710
Allegedly captured in Yosemite National Park
a few years later, the video shows what seems

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.710
to be two similar creatures… just taking
a stroll.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:49.159
Their overall gait looks even stranger than
in the first one, and their bodies appear

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.290
even more fabric like.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.399
In this footage, we can also see one Fresno
Nightcrawler appears much bigger than the

00:01:55.399 --> 00:01:56.399
other.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:59.670
This is a pattern consistent across many other
sightings and eyewitness testimony.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.189
There’s something about the dynamic which
almost seems like a parent and child… a

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:08.050
bizarre concept, but I admit I find it strangely
wholesome.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:13.060
And the most recent footage of these alleged
beings comes from Montana, holding the special

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.330
distinction of being the blurriest video of
them all.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:21.400
Here, we can barely make out what seems like
a single Fresno Nightcrawler sort of shimmy

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.260
into view… and then shimmy back into the
darkness outside of the camera’s radius.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.260
According to a dubious report attached to
the footage, a deer carcass was found nearby

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:35.100
the next morning, with the implication being
the Fresno Nightcrawler… somehow hunted

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.440
it down.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.430
Although likely intended to be frightening,
I find this addition really amusing — as

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.490
it makes me wonder how the creature was supposedly
able to kill a deer using nothing but its

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.590
spindly legs.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.210
It’s an image that’s going to stay with
me for sure.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.630
And that’s all the major pieces of footage
we have, although scattered eyewitness accounts

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.920
have also cropped up over the years.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.820
Thinking about all three of these supposed
pieces of ‘documentation,’ one thing in

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:04.890
particular I like about these alleged beings
is that they don’t seem to be camera shy.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:09.120
Most historic cryptids like bigfoot are usually
portrayed as being scared of being caught

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.970
on film — or at least skittish around humans
in general, which lends some credibility to

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.040
the idea that’s why we’ve never found
one.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.310
But in all the ‘footage’ we have, these
little dudes seem like they couldn’t care

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.450
less if someone is watching.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.850
They just stroll about wherever they please.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:31.940
In the footage from 2007, you can even hear
a dog barking and a car passing, but the Fresno

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.340
Nightcralwer just keeps on rolling, not a
care in the world.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.950
So, looking at all this so-called ‘evidence,’
what’s the most likely explanation behind

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:39.950
this footage?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.750
Well, as much as I’d like to say there’s
nothing about this footage at all that seems

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.070
like a hoax… that’s pretty clearly what
this is.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:51.770
Everything from the suspiciously blurry footage,
to the fact it’s difficult to confirm where

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:56.750
any of these videos actually originate from,
to the blunt fact the creatures in the video

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:02.020
move an awful lot like puppets with the wires
edited out is enough to raise a few eyebrows,

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.020
at the very least.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:07.910
But it’s a very fun idea for a hoax, and
one which I’m glad has produced so many

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:08.910
great interpretations.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:13.820
Still, it’s my duty as an archivist to assert
that the hoax-theory is by far the most reasonable

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.120
conclusion to draw from these videos.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:21.329
But, that’s no fun, so I’m going to take
a moment to talk about less likely, but far

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:24.680
more entertaining theories which have emerged
regarding what it is we’re seeing in this

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.729
footage.

00:04:25.729 --> 00:04:29.190
And prepare yourself: some of these get wild.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:34.479
Perhaps most convincingly, I’ve heard theories
that although the videos are obviously faked,

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:37.669
some eyewitnesses might have actually seen
something real.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:43.080
Not a cryptid, but a type of crane, which
they mistook for a skinny, two-legged otherworldly

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.080
being.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.030
At first, this explanation seemed odd to me,
but the more footage I looked at — the more

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:52.340
I could see how late at night someone might
mistake the outline of a crane as something

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.000
nightcrawler-shaped.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.009
Getting into weirder territory, one of the
more common theories you can find is that

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:03.060
these little dudes are, in fact, visitors
from the vast expanse of the stars above.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.669
I would argue it seems, uh….

00:05:04.669 --> 00:05:09.830
unusual that aliens advanced enough for interplanetary
space travel would touch down only to take

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.110
a leisurely stroll.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.969
I’m not an alien so I can’t be certain
(hey, maybe they enjoy a nice walk just like

00:05:15.969 --> 00:05:21.379
we do?), but I wouldn’t exactly call any
of this footage… hard proof of extra-terrestrials.

00:05:21.379 --> 00:05:26.400
Beyond aliens, another relatively common theory
is that the Fresno Nightcrawlers are a hereby

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.680
undiscovered species of animal.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:34.490
It’s true that in the natural world, many
strange forms of life exist, but a mouthless,

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:39.160
armless, torso-less land animal herby unknown
to science despite moving at roughly 2 miles

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.780
an hour seems unlikely to say the least.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.419
Another biological explanation I’ve heard
put forward is that what we are seeing is

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:48.990
some sort of undiscovered species of fungus.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.120
A cool idea!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.770
I’m not an expert on fungus, but I don’t
feel I’m overstepping when I say I doubt

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:59.469
any strain of mushroom, no matter how fantastical,
is likely to go on a midnight walk.

00:05:59.469 --> 00:06:01.460
Although I wish they would, that would be
great.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:05.590
And the final theory I’d like to touch on
— and my personal favorite — is that what

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.860
we’re seeing in this footage looks like
pairs of pants because… that’s what they

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:10.860
are.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.210
Ghost pants, that is.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.180
Why would ethereal pants walk through the
mortal realm?

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.650
Who can say.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:20.259
Maybe they weren’t machine washable and
yet someone threw them in anyways, and now

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:24.639
they haunt the streets they used to walk when
they were attached to a human’s legs?

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:33.500
Maybe not the most likely theory, but definitely
the one I think is most fun, and most creative.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:39.569
In the end, regardless of their true authenticity,
Fresno Nightcrawlers can be real in our hearts.

00:06:39.569 --> 00:06:43.990
These little dudes might not look much like
real organisms, or real in general, but they

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:45.820
do look wonderful.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:46.960
Thanks for watching.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.580
If you liked this video, please lend your
support and like, subscribe, and hit the notification

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.490
icon to stay up to date on all things Curious.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.099
See you in the next video.

